WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.511
The Mock Turtle sighed deeply and wiped his eyes with his flippers.

2
00:00:05.512 --> 00:00:08.018
He looked at Alice and tried to speak.

3
00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:11.018
But he started sobbing instead.

4
00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:14.601
"Don't worry," the Gryphon said to Alice.

5
00:00:14.602 --> 00:00:17.241
"He's always like this."

6
00:00:17.242 --> 00:00:22.012
The Mock Turtle soon recovered and began to explain the lobster dance.

7
00:00:22.013 --> 00:00:26.877
"You probably haven't ever lived under the sea."

8
00:00:26.878 --> 00:00:29.736
"No, I haven't," Alice said.

9
00:00:29.737 --> 00:00:33.967
"And perhaps you've never been introduced to a lobster."

10
00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:38.730
Alice started to say that she had eaten a lobster but stopped.

11
00:00:38.731 --> 00:00:45.278
"So you don't know how delightful a lobster dance is," the Mock Turtle said.

12
00:00:45.279 --> 00:00:49.234
Alice shook her head. "No, I don't."

13
00:00:49.235 --> 00:00:51.959
The Gryphon joined the conversation.

14
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.260
"First, you stand in a line along the seashore."

15
00:00:56.261 --> 00:00:59.477
"Two lines," the Mock Turtle corrected him.

16
00:00:59.478 --> 00:01:04.401
"Then, after you've cleared all the jellyfish out of the way—"

17
00:01:04.402 --> 00:01:08.965
"That usually takes some time," the Gryphon interrupted.

18
00:01:08.966 --> 00:01:11.711
"You take two steps forward—"

19
00:01:11.712 --> 00:01:15.447
"With a lobster as a partner," the Gryphon said.

20
00:01:15.448 --> 00:01:18.352
"Of course," the Mock Turtle said.

21
00:01:18.353 --> 00:01:22.757
"You step forward twice, face your partner, and—"

22
00:01:22.758 --> 00:01:29.942
"Change lobsters," the Gryphon said. "Then you throw the lobsters—"

23
00:01:29.943 --> 00:01:34.274
"As far out to sea as you can," the Mock Turtle said.

24
00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:38.127
"And swim after them," the Gryphon said.

25
00:01:38.128 --> 00:01:46.318
"Then do a somersault in the sea!" The Mock Turtle danced wildly about.

26
00:01:46.319 --> 00:01:52.540
"And change lobsters again!" the Gryphon yelled at the top of his lungs.

27
00:01:52.541 --> 00:01:56.674
"Go back to land again," the Mock Turtle said.

28
00:01:56.675 --> 00:02:00.849
"And the first part of the dance is over."

29
00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:05.634
Both creatures had been jumping around while they described the dance.

30
00:02:05.635 --> 00:02:09.340
Now they sat down and looked at Alice.

31
00:02:09.341 --> 00:02:12.561
She wasn't sure how to react.

32
00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:16.940
"It must be a very pretty dance," she finally said.

33
00:02:16.941 --> 00:02:21.067
"Would you like to see some of it?" the Mock Turtle asked.

34
00:02:21.068 --> 00:02:22.841
"Oh yes!"

35
00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:28.298
"We can do the first part without lobsters," the Mock Turtle said to the Gryphon.

36
00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:30.691
"Do you want to sing?"

37
00:02:30.692 --> 00:02:36.637
"You should sing because I've forgotten the words," the Gryphon replied.

38
00:02:36.638 --> 00:02:47.192
So the Mock Turtle sang about a snail doing the lobster dance.

39
00:02:47.193 --> 00:02:55.744
The two creatures began to dance around Alice, sometimes stepping on her feet by mistake.

40
00:02:55.745 --> 00:03:00.729
When they finished dancing, Alice clapped.

41
00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:06.873
"Now we want to hear about some of your adventures," the Gryphon said.

42
00:03:06.874 --> 00:03:11.363
He and the Mock Turtle sat on either side of Alice.

43
00:03:11.364 --> 00:03:15.120
"Well, if you're sure you want to hear my story . . .

44
00:03:15.121 --> 00:03:20.644
First, I chased the White Rabbit and fell down the rabbit hole," she began.

45
00:03:20.645 --> 00:03:25.953
By the time she told them about meeting the Caterpillar, they looked bored.

46
00:03:25.954 --> 00:03:30.546
"That's enough of your story," the Gryphon said.

47
00:03:30.547 --> 00:03:33.425
"But I'm not at the end!" Alice said.

48
00:03:33.426 --> 00:03:37.491
Once again she thought how rude everyone was.

49
00:03:37.492 --> 00:03:42.139
"Let's try more of the lobster dance," the Gryphon said.

50
00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.800
He turned to Alice.

51
00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:47.583
"Or would you like the Mock Turtle to sing another song?"

52
00:03:47.584 --> 00:03:53.963
"Another song, please," Alice replied so quickly that the Gryphon frowned.

53
00:03:53.964 --> 00:03:56.071
"Well." He sniffed.

54
00:03:56.072 --> 00:04:00.914
"That's not what I'd have chosen. But if that's what you want . . . "

55
00:04:00.915 --> 00:04:03.170
The Gryphon looked at the Mock Turtle.

56
00:04:03.171 --> 00:04:07.533
"Sing 'Turtle Soup' for her, old fellow."

57
00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:14.171
The Mock Turtle sighed and began to sing a song in a voice choked with sobs.

58
00:04:14.172 --> 00:04:20.794
He was interrupted by a voice calling, "The trial's beginning!"

59
00:04:20.795 --> 00:04:22.934
"Come on!" the Gryphon cried.

60
00:04:22.935 --> 00:04:28.302
Without waiting for the Mock Turtle, he grabbed Alice by the hand and ran off.

61
00:04:28.303 --> 00:04:31.287
"Whose trial is it?" Alice asked.

62
00:04:31.288 --> 00:04:39.453
But the Gryphon only repeated, "Come on!" and ran faster.

